    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0520" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 761.94/113</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Guthrie to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-16T13:00:00+09:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 16, 1916, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Embassy’s telegram of July 16, 3 p.m. I am confidentially informed that it is
                    understood that there is included in the new Russo-Japanese convention a further
                    clause in which it is provided that after the present war Japanese troops will
                    be permitted largely to replace the Russian troops formerly stationed at
                    Manchuria.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guthrie</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
